<title>UK: India buys 255,000 tonnes diesel for January - trade.</title>
<headline>India buys 255,000 tonnes diesel for January - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) bought 255,000 tonnes of diesel for January delivery, traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>This compares to 520,000 tonnes awarded for December delivery and was well below traders' expectations.  </p>
<p>Traders said four cargoes would go the east coast and two to the west.</p>
<p>Of those cargoes going to the east, Total would supply one, Shell one and Mobil two.</p>
<p>For the west, Shell and Kuwait Petroleum Corp would supply one each, the traders said.</p>
</text>
